+# Design: knowledge bundle from authored Markdown
+
+## Goal
+
+Turn the content people author in the app (Markdown documents, glossary entries and
+colloquial names of one collection) into a `KnowledgeBundle` (`knowledge-bundle/v1`), so
+publishing can run the existing bundle import (`build_snapshot` / `ImportBundle`) unchanged.
+The same content must always give the same bundle, and therefore the same
+`bundle_digest`, so an unchanged collection is recognised as "no change" on import.
+
+## Scope
+
+Included:
+
+- A new framework-free domain module `pharma_agent.domain.corpus.authoring` with
+  `split_markdown`, `slugify`, `section_key`, `section_choices` and `build_bundle`.
+- Unit tests in `backend/tests/domain/corpus/test_authoring.py`.
+
+Unchanged:
+
+- The bundle format and validation (`domain/corpus/bundle.py`), the snapshot/import
+  (`domain/corpus/models.py`, `application/corpus/import_bundle.py`), chunking, identity,
+  storage, API and the authored-content models in `domain/corpus/source.py`.
+- No new dependencies; no I/O (the module neither reads nor writes files).
+
+## Interfaces
+
+```python
+# pharma_agent/domain/corpus/authoring.py
+
+@dataclass(frozen=True)
+class MarkdownSection:
+    heading: str
+    path: tuple[str, ...]        # enclosing headings incl. this one; () for the lead-in
+    ordinal: int                 # 1-based, among the kept sections of the document
+    blocks: tuple[BlockRecord, ...]
+
+def split_markdown(markdown: str, *, fallback_heading: str) -> list[MarkdownSection]: ...
+def slugify(text: str, *, max_length: int = 80) -> str: ...
+def section_key(document_key: str, path: Sequence[str]) -> str: ...
+def bundle_document_key(collection_key: str, document_key: str) -> str: ...
+def section_choices(
+    collection: Collection, documents: Sequence[SourceDocument]
+) -> list[tuple[str, str]]: ...
+def build_bundle(
+    collection: Collection,
+    documents: Sequence[SourceDocument],
+    glossary: Sequence[GlossaryEntry],
+    colloquial: Sequence[ColloquialMappingRecord],
+) -> KnowledgeBundle: ...
+```
+
+`Collection` comes from `domain.corpus.models`, `SourceDocument` from
+`domain.corpus.source`, the record types from `domain.corpus.bundle`.
+
+## Approach
+
+The module sits in the domain layer next to `source.py` (authored content) and `bundle.py`
+(the target format); it depends only on those and on `models.py`. An application service
+can later load content through `SourceRepository`, call `build_bundle` and pass the result
+to the import — nothing in this change wires that up.
+
+### `split_markdown`
+
+- Line based. A line opening a fence (```` ``` ```` or `~~~`, up to 3 spaces of indent)
+  toggles "inside code" until a closing fence of the same character that is at least as
+  long. Inside code, nothing is a heading or a table row; the lines are prose.
+- Headings are ATX headings: `#`–`######` followed by a space (or end of line); the
+  optional closing `#` sequence is removed and the text stripped. A heading with empty
+  text is treated as prose.
+- A stack of `(level, heading)` gives the path: a new heading pops entries with level
+  `>=` its own, then is pushed; `path` is the stack's headings.
+- Text before the first heading (or the whole document without headings) becomes a
+  section with `heading = fallback_heading` and `path = ()`. This is the only section
+  with an empty path ("the first section" of the spec when it is a lead-in).
+- Within a section, a run of consecutive lines whose stripped form starts with `|` is a
+  table block (`markdown` = the run's lines, right-stripped, joined by `\n`); a counter
+  across the whole document assigns `table_key` `t1`, `t2`, …. Text between tables is a
+  prose block with its text stripped; blank prose is skipped.
+- Sections without blocks are dropped; ordinals number kept sections from 1.
+- Line endings are normalised (`\r\n`, `\r` → `\n`).
+
+### `slugify` and `section_key`
+
+- `slugify`: NFKD-decompose, map `đ/Đ` to `d`, drop combining marks and remaining non-ASCII,
+  lowercase, replace each run of non-`[a-z0-9]` with `-`, strip `-`. Longer than
+  `max_length`: cut, then strip trailing `-`. `"Đường uống"` → `"duong-uong"`.
+- `section_key(document_key, path)` = `f"{document_key}#{'/'.join(slugify(p) for p in path)}"`,
+  or `f"{document_key}#body"` when `path` is empty. A heading whose slug is empty
+  (e.g. only punctuation) contributes `section` so the key keeps a part per level.
+
+### Keys and determinism
+
+- Bundle document key = `f"{collection.key}:{document.key}"` (`bundle_document_key`).
+  Section keys build on it, so chunk ids (hashed from section keys) never collide across
+  collections.
+- Two sections of a document with the same key (e.g. two `## Ghi chú` under the same
+  parent) would fail bundle validation; later ones get `-2`, `-3`, … appended in reading
+  order. `section_choices` and `build_bundle` share one helper, so they agree on keys.
+- `build_bundle`:
+  - documents sorted by bundle key; `DocumentRecord(key, kind, title,
+    source=SourceInfo(title=source_title, url=source_url))`;
+  - one `SectionRecord` per section, in document-key then ordinal order, with
+    `heading`, `context_path=list(path)`, `ordinal`, `blocks`; the fallback heading is the
+    document title;
+  - glossary copied as given;
+  - colloquial mappings in the given order, each with section keys that do not exist in
+    the bundle removed (a key already mapped by an earlier mapping is removed too, since
+    the bundle validation rejects a section mapped twice); mappings themselves are kept;
+  - manifest: `schema_version`, `collection=BundleCollection(key, title)`, a fixed
+    generator (`name="pharma-agent-authoring"`, `version="1"`, `build_id` = the content
+    digest), `source_digests={}`, the document and section counts, `files={}` (filled by
+    `write_bundle` if the bundle is ever written).
+  - No clock, random or ids: the output depends only on the inputs (document order
+    included, as documents are sorted).
+- `section_choices`: documents in the given order (the repository returns them ordered by
+  title), sections in reading order; label = `" › ".join([title, *path])`.
+
+## Testing
+
+`backend/tests/domain/corpus/test_authoring.py`, plain pytest, no I/O:
+
+- `slugify`: Vietnamese marks and `đ`, punctuation runs, `max_length` cutting, empty input.
+- `section_key`: path joining and the `#body` case.
+- `split_markdown`: heading paths and levels, lead-in fallback, no-heading document, fenced
+  headings ignored, empty sections dropped, ordinals, table runs with document-wide keys,
+  prose stripping.
+- `section_choices`: keys/labels in reading order, duplicate-heading suffixes.
+- `build_bundle`: document keys and sorting, section records, glossary passthrough,
+  colloquial filtering, manifest fields and counts, same digest for shuffled document
+  order, the bundle passes `write_bundle` validation and `build_snapshot` accepts it.
+- Then the full backend suite (`uv run pytest` in `backend/`).
